{"title":"Bretschneider's formula","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Suppose we have a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral\" title=\"Quadrilateral\">quadrilateral</a> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edges</a> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> (in that order) and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonals</a> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f06a183d1092b27328c12a97322763ac8db97a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" />. <b>Bretschneider's formula</b> states that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74fe9b4608c09a5f19b35410d84cf675a66a940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD]=\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{4p^2q^2-(b^2+d^2-a^2-c^2)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"353\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>It can be derived with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vector\" title=\"Vector\">vector</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bretschneider%27s_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose a quadrilateral has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82fb3cd5abda50c77cb511084bed8673403b32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}, \\vec{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"21\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/56792bbc0308bf387f6c8ad815a1562c17a0d0f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} + \\vec{c} + \\vec{d} = \\vec{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" /> and that the diagonals of the quadrilateral are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114c8249230f212d372231c81dea87788c42f414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{p} = \\vec{b} + \\vec{c} = -\\vec{a} - \\vec{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee53869afb684e8f20fbdb93cd45f5d6deb8d319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{q} = \\vec{a} + \\vec{b} = -\\vec{c} - \\vec{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />. The area of any such quadrilateral is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66ada088458f04a417a2584710af753561adec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} |\\vec{p} \\times \\vec{q}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/8381820a9f5ac8713dab6aacab7282b165a28e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\frac{1}{2} |\\vec{p} \\times \\vec{q}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lagrange%27s_Identity\" title=\"Lagrange&#39;s Identity\">Lagrange's Identity</a> states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1edefc699697c5dba07a4f8d8cdcd6c107c5b502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\vec{a}|^2|\\vec{b}|^2-(\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})^2=|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|^2 \\implies \\sqrt{|\\vec{a}|^2|\\vec{b}|^2-(\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})^2}=|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"474\" height=\"32\" />. Therefore:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636d33630f3466ebeaee1280893deef28fd1895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{|\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - (\\vec{p} \\cdot \\vec{q})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"200\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79fe2a581182e39b035765c63949e60cb9f5eb04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - (2 \\vec{p} \\cdot \\vec{q})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9ccf2a4bc6104e21eeda53e7cbbb7b7d4fe7047b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [2 (\\vec{b} + \\vec{c}) \\cdot (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b})]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"280\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd10bed20a058d3d09fb72d3daedceaa3722307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [2 \\vec{b} \\cdot (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) + 2 \\vec{c} \\cdot (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b})]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"342\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb3346ccc404f33b51b30ea40611de912046b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [-2 \\vec{b} \\cdot (\\vec{c} + \\vec{d}) + 2 \\vec{c} \\cdot (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b})]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"356\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af05bc30058c961a26aa5d285509ea384c1e01c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [-2 \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{c} - 2 \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{d} + 2 \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{c} + 2 \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{c}]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/7588ef9fe40e58b9b4b50204f9f36cb37b06da53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [2 \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{c} - 2 \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{d}]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"253\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809d0ee15c6a549f26a9787ad3fa3108dd0fc1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - ([(\\vec{a} + \\vec{c})\\cdot(\\vec{a} + \\vec{c}) - \\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{a} - \\vec{c}\\cdot\\vec{c}] - [(\\vec{b} + \\vec{d})\\cdot(\\vec{b} + \\vec{d}) - \\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{b} - \\vec{d}\\cdot\\vec{d}])^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"650\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9a0e6892f0904d04edeccf6fc479f026971989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [|\\vec{b}|^2 + |\\vec{d}|^2 - |\\vec{a}|^2 - |\\vec{c}|^2 + (\\vec{a} + \\vec{c})\\cdot(\\vec{a} + \\vec{c}) - (\\vec{b} + \\vec{d})\\cdot(\\vec{b} + \\vec{d})]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"609\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef812fd4a088fe06d41088b1b9352db61e9b9714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [|\\vec{b}|^2 + |\\vec{d}|^2 - |\\vec{a}|^2 - |\\vec{c}|^2 + |\\vec{a} + \\vec{c}|^2 - |\\vec{b} + \\vec{d}|^2]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"482\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d937b4aa44995ee24f87d0ef66ecdbc567bcfd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [|\\vec{b}|^2 + |\\vec{d}|^2 - |\\vec{a}|^2 - |\\vec{c}|^2 + |\\vec{a} + \\vec{c}|^2 - |-(\\vec{a} + \\vec{c})|^2]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"519\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a0661d14ddd63a4eff01539fbc07ac27044273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4 |\\vec{p}|^2|\\vec{q}|^2 - [|\\vec{b}|^2 + |\\vec{d}|^2 - |\\vec{a}|^2 - |\\vec{c}|^2]^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"325\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Then if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caae136b98922d4260db50069eb107777b1fbb1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\vec{a}|, |\\vec{b}|, |\\vec{c}|, |\\vec{d}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"22\" /> (and are thus the side lengths) while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f06a183d1092b27328c12a97322763ac8db97a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" /> represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4eaf19210e4c17103aeecd53ce6b351d0645fe4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\vec{p}|, |\\vec{q}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> (and are thus the diagonal lengths), the area of a quadrilateral is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60dc4dbcb38afe751b3438020e7edec259fdf9a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K = \\frac{1}{4} \\sqrt{4p^2q^2 - (b^2 + d^2 - a^2 - c^2)^2}\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bretschneider%27s_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Brahmagupta&#39;s formula\">Brahmagupta's formula</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234252\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 148/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6815/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1937:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234252 and revision id 145879. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}